{"name":"Regatta","hex":"#5382bb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"regatta","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A series of boat races, or sometimes a single race.","A striped cotton fabric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regatta"}],"entries":[{"title":"Regatta (clothing)","blocks":[{"text":"Regatta is a British clothing brand based in Manchester. It is part of the privately owned Regatta Group, which also consists of Regatta Great Outdoors, Craghoppers, Dare2b, and Regatta Professional. The brand sells through major outdoor retail chains, through its own stores and concessions, and through e-commerce."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a2/Regatta_Clothing_logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regatta_(clothing)","wikidata":"Q9305279"},{"title":"Boat racing","blocks":[{"text":"Boat racing (Regatta) is a sport in which boats, or other types of watercraft, race on water. Boat racing powered by oars is recorded as having occurred in ancient Egypt, and it is likely that people have engaged in races involving boats and other water-borne craft for as long as such watercraft have existed."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boat_racing","wikidata":"Q11344830"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Eights_at_Head_of_the_Schuylkill.jpg/500px-Eights_at_Head_of_the_Schuylkill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Eights_at_Head_of_the_Schuylkill.jpg/500px-Eights_at_Head_of_the_Schuylkill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Head of the Schuylkill Regatta","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEights_at_Head_of_the_Schuylkill.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Rowing%2C_Lucie